 /**
- * How Remix interop handles reach OpenGL on each platform. Everything else in
- * {@link GlInterop} is platform-neutral.
+ * How Remix interop handles reach OpenGL on each platform, and the rules for
+ * owning them. GlInterop asks this class instead of branching on the platform.
  *
- * <p>Windows: the {@code InteropInfo} handle fields carry Win32 handles,
- * imported with {@code EXT_memory_object_win32} and {@code EXT_semaphore_win32}.
- * This is unchanged.
+ * <p>Windows (unchanged): the {@code InteropInfo} handle fields carry Win32
+ * handles, imported with {@code EXT_*_win32}; the semaphores are NV timeline
+ * semaphores driven by wait/signal values; an image is identified by its handle.
  *
- * <p>Linux: the handle fields are assumed to carry opaque POSIX file descriptors
- * ({@code VK_EXTERNAL_*_HANDLE_TYPE_OPAQUE_FD_BIT}), imported with
- * {@code EXT_memory_object_fd} and {@code EXT_semaphore_fd}. A successful GL
- * import takes ownership of the descriptor it is given. The runtime is assumed
- * to keep owning the descriptors it reports, and to report the same descriptor
- * while an allocation is unchanged. GlInterop's change detection compares handle
- * values, so this class imports a {@code dup()} and the runtime's descriptor
- * stays valid. If the interop work settles on the runtime handing the client a
- * fresh descriptor on every call instead, import the descriptor itself in
- * {@link #importFd} and stop comparing handle values in GlInterop.
+ * <p>Linux, following the runtime's contract (PORTING_NOTES, Phase D step 5):
+ * <ul>
+ *   <li>Every non-zero handle field of every {@code dxvk_GetInteropInfo} call is
+ *       a fresh opaque file descriptor that the caller owns. Each one is either
+ *       imported, which hands it to GL, or closed with {@link #release}.</li>
+ *   <li>Descriptor numbers say nothing about identity, so an image is the same
+ *       image while its size, format and allocation size are unchanged.</li>
+ *   <li>The semaphores are binary: no NV timeline objects or values. The runtime
+ *       signals dxvkDone once per Present and never waits on clientDone.</li>
+ *   <li>The image is {@code VK_IMAGE_TILING_OPTIMAL}, so the GL texture needs
+ *       {@code GL_TEXTURE_TILING_EXT = GL_OPTIMAL_TILING_EXT} before its storage
+ *       is bound to the memory.</li>
+ * </ul>
  */
